= Constant-product market maker — Technical =

Ignoring fees, reserves x and y satisfy xy=k. The instantaneous reserve-curve price magnitude is |dy/dx|=y/x. For a finite input Δx, the required output moves the state from (x,y) to (x+Δx,y-Δy) on the curve; fees alter the effective input and reserve accounting.

== Modeling / security cautions ==
* constant-product market maker ≠ every AMM
* x·y=k model ≠ zero price impact
* invariant ≠ fixed market price

== References ==
* BIS, “Trading in the DeFi era: automated market-maker” (2021).
* Guillermo Angeris & Tarun Chitra, “Improved Price Oracles: Constant Function Market Makers” (2020).
* Uniswap v2 Core whitepaper (2020), as a canonical deployed constant-product design.
